2.1. This licence is addressed only to the persons described in section 3. Its full text must be available for review before an act constituting acceptance. You accept this licence when, after being given that opportunity, you do any of the following with the Software:
- download it;
- install it;
- run it;
- copy it;
- modify it;
- pass on copies or make it available to the public under clause 6.3.

The agreement between you and the Licensor is concluded on acceptance.

2.2. If a person does not meet the conditions of section 3, that person's acts with the Software do not constitute acceptance of this licence, and that person acquires no rights in the Software.

2.3. By starting to use the Software you represent to the Licensor that, as of the date you start using it, you meet the conditions of section 3. This representation is deemed repeated on each day of use, except during a transition period agreed under clause 7.1, when you represent that you comply with the terms of that written agreement.

## 3. Who may use the Software free of charge

3.1. Rights under this licence are granted only to the following persons:
- a legal entity or sole trader whose Group is a Qualifying Group, for Internal Purposes;
- an individual, for personal, educational and research purposes not connected with business activity.

3.2. A legal entity or sole trader whose Group is not a Qualifying Group may ask the Licensor for permission to evaluate the Software. The Licensor states the period and terms of the evaluation in a written permission. Without such permission or a Commercial Licence, that person may not use the Software.

## 4. Rights granted

4.1. The Licensor grants you a non-exclusive licence to use the Software for the purposes set out in section 3 in the following ways:

1. reproduction — installing, running, storing in computer memory and copying;
2. modification and creation of Derivatives — only for your own use in accordance with section 6;
3. distribution of unmodified copies and making the unmodified Software available to the public — only in accordance with clause 6.3.

4.2. The licence is granted **free of charge**.

4.3. Territory: worldwide.

4.4. Term: the full term of the copyright in the Software, unless the licence terminates earlier under section 9.

4.5. This licence grants no rights beyond the use it expressly permits. Further rights may be granted under a Commercial Licence or written evaluation permission under clause 3.2. Rights and exceptions provided directly by applicable law remain available to the extent required by that law.

4.6. Group members may use the Software accepted by any one of them for the Internal Purposes of the whole Group. Each Group member that uses the Software is deemed to have accepted this licence.

## 5. What requires a Commercial Licence

Without a Commercial Licence you may not:

5.1. use the Software as a legal entity or sole trader whose Group is not a Qualifying Group — except for evaluation with the Licensor's permission (clause 3.2); an individual's personal use under clause 3.1 does not depend on the size of the Group;

5.2. Provide the Software as a Service — **including if your Group is a Qualifying Group**;

5.3. sell, rent out or otherwise distribute the Software for a fee;

5.4. distribute Derivatives or otherwise give them to persons outside your Group;

5.5. grant sublicences;

5.6. remove or alter any copyright, licence or Licensor notices contained in the Software;

5.7. add to the Software or a Derivative any means specifically designed to violate the restrictions of this licence or conceal such a violation. Ordinary information security, confidentiality and network isolation measures are not, by themselves, a violation.

## 6. Modifying the Software and passing on copies

6.1. You may modify the Software and create Derivatives only for use for the purposes set out in section 3, including within your Group.

6.2. You may not distribute or publish Derivatives or otherwise give them to persons outside your Group.

6.3. You may pass on the unmodified Software to other persons and make it available for download on the Internet only together with the full text of this licence and the NOTICE file, free of charge and without additional terms. The recipient receives rights directly from the Licensor if the recipient meets the conditions of section 3 and accepts this licence under section 2.

6.4. You may engage a contractor to install, configure, modify and administer the Software solely on your behalf and for your benefit on your infrastructure or infrastructure under your control. Such contractor access to the Software, including Derivatives, is not Providing as a Service, sublicensing or a transfer of a Derivative outside the Group. The contractor must comply with the applicable restrictions of this licence and may not use the copy independently, give it to others or retain it after the engagement. You must ensure the contractor complies with these conditions. A contractor hosting the Software to provide it to customers as a service does not fall within this exception.

## 7. Compliance with the free-use conditions

7.1. If you use the Software as a legal entity or sole trader and your Group ceases to be a Qualifying Group — including because you have become part of a larger group — further use of the Software is permitted only under a Commercial Licence. If you need time to move to a Commercial Licence, contact the Licensor; a transition period may be agreed in writing.

7.2. If the Licensor has grounds to believe that your Group is not a Qualifying Group, it may send you a request if you use the Software as a legal entity or sole trader. Within 30 calendar days after receiving the request, you must provide a written confirmation, signed by an authorised person, that your Group is a Qualifying Group, stating its Headcount and Revenue. If the confirmation is insufficient, the Licensor may request supporting documents relevant to calculating Headcount and Revenue; you must respond within 30 calendar days after receiving that request. If no response is received by the deadline, the Licensor will send a repeated request warning of the consequences under clause 9.2. The Licensor may also check information about Group members in public registers and other public sources. The Licensor will keep the information confidential and use it only to verify compliance with this licence.

7.3. The Licensor publishes explanations of this licence (FAQ) with examples. The Licensor will not make claims regarding use that the explanations expressly describe as permitted at the time of such use. If the explanations conflict with this licence, the licence prevails.

## 8. Liability for use beyond the licence

8.1. Use of copyright-protected parts of the Software beyond the rights granted, including after termination, without another lawful basis may constitute copyright infringement under applicable law. Subject to that law, the following uses are outside the rights granted unless authorised by a separate agreement, written permission from the Licensor or law:
- use by a person who does not meet the conditions of section 3;
- use after your Group has ceased to be a Qualifying Group, without a Commercial Licence and without an agreed transition period;
- Providing as a Service;
- distribution of Derivatives.

The Licensor may pursue the remedies available to a copyright owner under applicable law and may enforce its contractual rights under this licence. Statutory damages or compensation are available only where applicable law provides for them and its requirements are met.

8.2. If an agreement under this licence was concluded, for a breach of clauses 5.1–5.4 you must pay an amount equal to the fee for the relevant use, to the extent enforceable under applicable law. For Internal Purposes by the Group category described in clause 14.2, the base fee in that clause applies. Otherwise, the public price list in force when the breach began applies.

For a continuing breach, the fee is prorated to the number of calendar days of the breach relative to the period covered by the fee. An annual fee is calculated separately for each calendar year of the breach: the annual fee is multiplied by the number of breach days in that year and divided by the number of calendar days in that year. If the Group's category changes, the periods are calculated separately for each category using the tariffs in force when the breach began. A one-off transfer requires a separate tariff for that transfer.

The price list must unambiguously determine the total amount for the relevant use and Group category, including the treatment of applicable VAT, GST or similar transaction taxes. A price stated as "from" or "by agreement" without a determinate calculation formula does not support a payment under this clause. Breaches of clauses 5.2–5.4 require a separate public tariff for the relevant use; an internal-use tariff cannot be substituted. If no applicable determinate tariff exists, no contractual payment under this clause is due for that breach; remedies available under law remain unaffected.

Later price changes do not increase the amount. The payment is credited against damages or compensation for the same breach; double recovery is not permitted. Payment does not authorise continued use. If no agreement was concluded, this contractual payment does not apply. Nothing in this clause overrides mandatory limits on contractual remedies or creates an entitlement to a payment prohibited by applicable law.

8.3. You are liable for any inaccuracy of the representation under clause 2.3.

8.4. Your obligations under sections 5 to 8 apply to the whole Software. If any part is held not to be protected by copyright, obligations concerning that part remain contractual only where an agreement was concluded and to the extent permitted by applicable law. This clause creates no copyright in unprotected material and does not bind persons who are not parties to the agreement.

## 9. Termination

9.1. This licence terminates automatically, without notice, when you breach its terms, except where clause 9.2 provides a specific procedure. Failure to provide information under clause 7.2 results in termination only under that procedure. This clause applies to the extent permitted by applicable law.

9.2. The licence also terminates automatically:
- when you use the Software as a legal entity or sole trader and your Group ceases to be a Qualifying Group, unless a Commercial Licence has been concluded or a transition period has been agreed under clause 7.1; if a transition period has been agreed, the free licence terminates at its end unless a Commercial Licence has been concluded;
- if you fail to provide the confirmation or supporting documents requested under clause 7.2 within 30 calendar days after receiving a repeated request warning of termination.

9.3. On termination you must stop using the Software and destroy your copies of it, except copies you are required by law to retain. Termination does not release liability for breaches already committed or end the Licensor's confidentiality obligation under clause 7.2.

9.4. Termination of this licence for one Licensee does not terminate the rights of persons who lawfully received the unmodified Software from that Licensee and who meet the conditions of section 3.

