16.3. If you do not agree with a new version that applies to previously obtained Software under clause 16.2, you must stop using it, except as provided in clause 16.4.

16.4. For a Licensee whose use is not connected with business activity, changes to an existing agreement require consent unless applicable law permits otherwise. Until consent is given, previously obtained Software remains subject to the previous terms; refusal of the new terms does not by itself terminate that licence. In all cases, new terms do not change the legal treatment of use that occurred before those terms took effect for the Licensee.

16.5. Notwithstanding clauses 16.2 and 16.3, a new version of this licence does not make chargeable the use of a version of the Software that you obtained before the new version was published. A person who met the conditions of section 3 of the licence version under which that version of the Software was obtained may continue to use it free of charge for the purposes set out in that section for as long as that person continues to meet those conditions. Those conditions are read together with the definitions in section 1 of that licence version. In all other respects the new version applies to that use as provided in clauses 16.2 to 16.4.

